From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0320-rebase-01-compact-hmma.patch

Source: 0320-rebase-01-compact-hmma.patch
Moved by hand: a comment hunk moved by upstream's movie note; code hunks unchanged

shader: EDEN_NX2_TENSOR=compact runs HMMA through one shared software helper

Port of Djihads80/Eglantine e88024e6b0 (Duck912, branch scratch/oot-shader-lab, 2026-11-05), which
ports zortos293/Lichii #5 by Mattscreative in its form from 8cd5c6a44b. GPL-3.0-or-later, as the
core. Credit lines of the source commit: Co-authored-by Mattscreative, Zortos.

Why: the source commit says Ocarina of Time draws its final image through an 11-program network
after the tonemap, and measured Kokiri Forest median luma ~0.29 with the stand-in against ~0.10 with
the network, "flat and far too bright". run61 logs 11 "native matrix multiply" rejections: ten in one
burst at 34 s (code at 0x216c8...), one at 90.9 s from another region (0x1148bd5300). Only the count
matches; the source names no addresses, so these being its 11 programs is a guess.

run60 is the one console measure (EDEN_NX2_TENSOR=1, HMMA_NATIVE, the same arithmetic as this form):
- Its ten compute pipelines were translated by 34.9 s, then one frame took 15.66 s. That timer leaves
  out the driver compile, which runs on workers, so the stall is likely the compile, not proven.
- Frames came back at 17.2 fps (worst 61 ms) where run61 holds 60: about 40 ms a frame, one 5 s
  sample. This form does the same products, so do not expect it to be cheaper on the GPU.
- At the third heap report the heap held 2188 MiB against 1174 in run61, with 907 and 943 in use. Run
  with EDEN_HEAP_KEEP_ARENAS=1, that extra GiB is not given back. Whether this form costs it too is
  not known.
- No frame after about 55 s, no crash report, and the log runs on to 146 s with most guest threads
  unchanged. Cause unknown. It came after the pipelines were built, so compile cost does not explain it.

RADV inlines every function (nir_inline_functions, radv_shader.c), so DontInline does not hold there:
each HMMA gets its own copy of the helper's loop, 207 lines of SPIR-V. The gain over HMMA_NATIVE on
the console is a rolled loop per site, not one helper per program. How much that cuts the compile is
not known.

HMMA now lowers to TENSOR_MUL_ADD, a Maxwell-encoded pseudo-instruction (bit 48 marks it, bit 49
selects K = 8). The translator makes an IR TensorMulAdd; the SPIR-V backend defines one loop helper
per K depth and program and calls it at each site: same lane mapping, f32 sums and half rounding
after every eight products as the expansion, with subgroup shuffles. GLSL and GLASM don't have it.
A guarded HMMA keeps HMMA_NATIVE.

Changed from the source: no per-title default and no compact_tensor option. It runs only with
EDEN_NX2_TENSOR=compact, set by hand; unset, nothing changes. No cache version bump, as in 0043: the
lowered code is the pipeline key (Analyze hashes it). The source's check that compute shaders are
made 32 threads wide is gone with its per-title gate: vk_compute_pipeline.cpp asks for 32 when a
program uses warp operations, RADV offers that from GFX10, and the helper masks lane & ~31 anyway.
spirv_software_matrix.cpp, the source's test, is left out.

Checked off the console: spirv-val accepts the helper's SPIR-V for K = 8 and 16, made by this
emit_spirv_tensor.cpp through a stand-in for sirit's calls, not real sirit. A C copy of round_half
matches _Float16 on all 2^32 float patterns (NaNs skipped). Neither ran on a GPU.

Core patch. Nothing here has run on a console.

